@startuml
title T12-WF04 — AI CRM Follow-up Agent
start
:01 | RabbitMQ Trigger\nconsume one lead.follow_up.triggered event with required executionId target field; keep this as the single primary trigger for that execution, not a parallel webhook.;
:02 | Code: Validate Execution Request\nvalidate execution, enrollment, step, channel and correlation IDs.;
:03 | HTTP Request: Get Follow-up Context\nfetch the enrollment, Lead and step from NestJS.;
:04 | Code: Check Eligibility\nverify active enrollment, due time, next step and duplicate-execution safeguards.;
:05 | Code: Render Message Payload\nprepare recipient, subject and content from approved templates.;
:06 | HTTP Request: Backend Send Message\ncall the NestJS Communication API; actual email/provider delivery stays in backend.;
:07 | Code: Normalize Delivery Result\nclassify the result as SUCCESS, RETRYABLE_FAILURE or PERMANENT_FAILURE.;
:08 | HTTP Request: Execution Callback\nrecord the normalized delivery result through the authenticated backend callback.;
:09 | Code: Prepare Execution Outcome\nretain the canonical delivery status and correlation/idempotency keys for the next decision.;
if (10 | Delivery succeeded?) then (yes)
  :11 | HTTP Request: Backend Advance/Complete\nadvance the step or complete the enrollment transactionally after confirmed delivery.;
else (no)
  :12 | HTTP Request: Backend Handle Delivery Failure\nbackend applies bounded retry for retryable errors or records terminal failure; never advance a failed delivery.;
endif
stop
@enduml
